gxde-kwin-x11 for Debian
------------------------

The runtime binary package is named gxde-kwin-x11-6 so that it does not replace
the existing GXDE 5.x package named gxde-kwin-x11. The fork's files are under
their own namespace and do not conflict with the existing KWin files.

Debian's libkdecorations3-6 package declares a Breaks against KDecoration 2.
This source therefore emits libgxde-kdecorations3-6 with the same Qt 6 public
library but without that cross-major-version Breaks. It still conflicts with
the distribution libkdecorations3-6 package because both own the same Qt 6
library file. The KDecoration 2 runtime remains installed and usable by the
existing GXDE window manager.

The source still compiles shared Wayland protocol and support code used by the
KWin core library. This is not a Wayland compositor build: neither
kwin_wayland nor gxde-kwin_wayland is a CMake target or an installed file.

The package build disables upstream tests and screen-locker integration, then
explicitly enables only the gxde-kwin_x11 executable backend.
